import Native

{-
   Whirlpool's compression, over eight 64-bit lanes - the form for a machine that has them.

   See `Whirlpool.yana` for the table, the state and why there are two of these. The selector on this
   file is the whole of what chooses it.
-}

{-
   The table and the round constants, at the width this implementation works in.

   They live beside the compression that reads them rather than in `Whirlpool.yana`, so that a
   program carries one spelling of them and not two: this file and `Whirlpool.js.yana` are never both
   selected, and 2 KB of table the chosen one cannot read is 2 KB of dead image.

   `I64` and read through `bitcast`, which is `Float/Ryu.native.yana`'s trick and is there for the
   same reason: more than half of these values have their top bit set, an integer literal is read at
   `Long`, and written unsigned they would not fit. The `bitcast` per read folds to nothing.
-}
